Z||000000||V6pack||02-25-2000||01:01 PM||||<BR>Hi, guys/girls.  I have GT on which the radiator fan runs from start up to shut down.  What is the likely cause?  Sensor? <P>Ran a topic search with no luck. Any ideas?<BR>TIA..v6pack||||reg||2
Z||000001||theogre||02-25-2000||04:31 PM||||AC or heat on? that will do it.<P>Otherwise look for stuck relay, bad engine temp switch, short to ground in control wire. <P>Bad AC control in dash could do it. just unplug the whole control unit to test that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wwh0001||02-25-2000||04:49 PM||||Has it always done this. The prior owner may have grounded the fan switch , either due to a faulty switch, or  simply wanted the fan on all the time to cool the engine. would look at the fan switch first. These fan switches go bad often. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||02-25-2000||06:30 PM||||If it has done it since you've owned it it is also possible the previous owner installed a hidden switch to turn it own. Look around under the dash.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||02-25-2000||09:57 PM||||look at the relay, the one that is on the front firewall, or in front of the lght, check if there is a wire that is going from that relay to the fan, on mine someone did this, i disconnected it and presto. now it comes on when it's suposed to.good luck,AL. ||||reg||14
Z||000005||V6pack||02-25-2000||11:05 PM||||Good suggestions guys!  Judging the PO by the car he sent me and all that was/is wrong with it......I'd better go "strange" wire hunting in the morning. That would have been his solution to an overheating problem....mickey mouse it.<P>I'll go down the good list of stuff you mentioned if I don't find a "mystery" wire.  But... I bet I do find one.   I'll let you guys know.<BR>Thanks for the help.<BR>v6pack||||reg||14
